* ============================================================================
* CSS4J-4026 - 4-terminal (Kelvin) current-sense shunt, simple model (2026-09-28)
* The KiCad part R1: 1 mOhm, pins 1 = F1 (force, Vin), 2 = S1 (sense, ISNS_P), 3 = S2 (sense, ISNS_N),
* 4 = F2 (force, rsense_lo).  The load current flows F1 -> F2 through the element; the sense pins tap the element's
* own ends, so the INA sees only the element drop, not the pad/solder drops (which are not modelled).
* The sense leads get 1 mOhm each; only the INA input bias current (tens of uA) flows in them.
* NOT MODELLED: tolerance, TCR, inductance, self-heating.
* ============================================================================
.SUBCKT CSS4J_4026 F1 S1 S2 F2 PARAMS: R=1m
RE F1 F2 {R}
RS1 F1 S1 1m
RS2 F2 S2 1m
.ENDS CSS4J_4026
